//RS /// `jet repl [<file>.jet]` — interactive REPL session (E2-M18, D-REPL3=A).
//RS /// `project_dir` sets the base for `:load` paths and (eventually) import
//RS /// context (D-REPL10=A sandbox; `--project <dir>` enables project mode).
//RS ///
//RS /// #2038: a positional `<file>.jet` is a session preload — its definitions
//RS /// become available in turn 1 through the one ratified file-into-session
//RS /// mechanism, `:load` (D-REPL15=B); `fn run` is NOT invoked, because running a
//RS /// program is `jet run`. A path that isn't there is refused here, before the
//RS /// banner, exactly the way `run_dev` above refuses one (E2105). Silently
//RS /// starting an empty session was the bug.
//RS pub(crate) fn run_repl(
//RS     project_dir: Option<&str>,
//RS     preload: Option<&str>,
//RS     allow: &[String],
//RS     deny: &[String],
